{
 "id": "2026-10-26-simpsons-paradox",
 "topic": "Simpson's paradox: kidney stone treatments (weighted averages)",
 "subject": "statistics",
 "hook_type": "visual surprise",
 "caption": "Treatment A beats B for small stones (93% vs 87%) and for large stones (73% vs 69%), yet B wins overall (83% vs 78%). Overall rate is a weighted average, and A was given mostly to the harder large-stone cases. Data from Charig et al., 1986.\n\nSave this before you trust your next average.\n\n#statistics #simpsonsparadox #datascience #probability #math #stem #dataanalysis #research",
 "cover_at": 1.0,
 "hook": "A treatment can win in every group and still lose overall.",
 "sub": "Real kidney stone data.",
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "A 1986 study compared two kidney stone treatments. First, patients with small stones: the success rates.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "sm",
     "tex": [
      "\\text{small stones}"
     ],
     "size": 48,
     "color": "dim",
     "at": [
      0,
      5.6
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "a1",
     "tex": [
      "A:",
      "\\tfrac{81}{87}",
      "=",
      "93\\%"
     ],
     "size": 64,
     "at": [
      0,
      4.6
     ],
     "colors": {
      "0": "blue",
      "3": "blue"
     }
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "b1",
     "tex": [
      "B:",
      "\\tfrac{234}{270}",
      "=",
      "87\\%"
     ],
     "size": 64,
     "next_to": "a1",
     "buff": 0.3,
     "colors": {
      "0": "teal",
      "3": "teal"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "A wins. Now patients with large stones, which are harder to treat.",
   "do": [
    {
     "indicate": "a1",
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "lg",
     "tex": [
      "\\text{large stones}"
     ],
     "size": 48,
     "color": "dim",
     "next_to": "b1",
     "buff": 0.5
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "a2",
     "tex": [
      "A:",
      "\\tfrac{192}{263}",
      "=",
      "73\\%"
     ],
     "size": 64,
     "next_to": "lg",
     "buff": 0.3,
     "colors": {
      "0": "blue",
      "3": "blue"
     }
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "b2",
     "tex": [
      "B:",
      "\\tfrac{55}{80}",
      "=",
      "69\\%"
     ],
     "size": 64,
     "next_to": "a2",
     "buff": 0.3,
     "colors": {
      "0": "teal",
      "3": "teal"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "A wins again. A is better for small stones and better for large stones. So A is better, right?",
   "do": [
    {
     "indicate": "a2",
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "sfx": "tick"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Now pool everyone together and compute the overall success rates.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "ta",
     "tex": [
      "A:",
      "\\frac{81+192}{87+263}",
      "=",
      "\\frac{273}{350}",
      "=",
      "78\\%"
     ],
     "size": 60,
     "at": [
      0,
      3.6
     ],
     "colors": {
      "0": "blue",
      "5": "red"
     }
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "tb",
     "tex": [
      "B:",
      "\\frac{234+55}{270+80}",
      "=",
      "\\frac{289}{350}",
      "=",
      "83\\%"
     ],
     "size": 60,
     "next_to": "ta",
     "buff": 0.5,
     "colors": {
      "0": "teal",
      "5": "green"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "B wins overall. A wins in every group, and loses in total. Both are true.",
   "do": [
    {
     "sfx": "thud"
    },
    {
     "circle": "tb"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The catch is who got which treatment. A was used mostly on large stones, B mostly on small ones.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "ttl",
     "tex": [
      "\\text{number of patients}"
     ],
     "size": 52,
     "color": "dim",
     "at": [
      0,
      5.6
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "bars",
     "name": "br",
     "values": [
      87,
      263,
      270,
      80
     ],
     "labels": [
      "A small",
      "A large",
      "B small",
      "B large"
     ],
     "colors": [
      "blue",
      "blue",
      "teal",
      "teal"
     ],
     "max": 300,
     "step": 100,
     "size": [
      7.2,
      4.2
     ],
     "at": [
      0,
      2.9
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Large stones are harder for both, so A's overall rate is dragged down by its mix of patients.",
   "do": [
    {
     "indicate": "br",
     "color": "yellow"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Overall success is a weighted average. The weights are the share of patients in each group.",
   "do": [
    {
     "sfx": "riser"
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "wa",
     "tex": [
      "A:",
      "0.25",
      "(93\\%)",
      "+",
      "0.75",
      "(73\\%)",
      "\\approx",
      "78\\%"
     ],
     "size": 52,
     "at": [
      0,
      3.6
     ],
     "colors": {
      "1": "yellow",
      "4": "yellow",
      "7": "red"
     }
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "wb",
     "tex": [
      "B:",
      "0.77",
      "(87\\%)",
      "+",
      "0.23",
      "(69\\%)",
      "\\approx",
      "83\\%"
     ],
     "size": 52,
     "next_to": "wa",
     "buff": 0.5,
     "colors": {
      "1": "yellow",
      "4": "yellow",
      "7": "green"
     }
    },
    {
     "sfx": "ding"
    },
    {
     "make": "box",
     "name": "bx",
     "around": "wb",
     "color": "green"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Different weights, same rates. Stone size drives both the choice and the outcome, so compare within each size.",
   "do": [
    {
     "hide": "bx"
    },
    {
     "indicate": [
      "wa",
      "wb"
     ],
     "color": "yellow"
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
